{"duration_api_ms":147476,"stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"eeef7da4-8396-4a27-a9ee-ae3deeb7bc5c","total_cost_usd":0.7250348,"usage":{"input_tokens":36,"cache_creation_input_tokens":40147,"cache_read_input_tokens":696974,"output_tokens":13216,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":5870},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":40147,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1157,"cache_read_input_tokens":53906,"cache_creation_input_tokens":564,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":564},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"modelUsage":{"claude-opus-5-5":{"inputTokens":36,"outputTokens":13216,"cacheReadInputTokens":696974,"cacheCreationInputTokens":40147,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.7250348,"contextWindow":1000000,"maxOutputTokens":128000,"thinkingTokens":5870,"cacheCreationEphemeral5mInputTokens":0,"cacheCreationEphemeral1hInputTokens":40147,"canonicalModel":"claude-opus-5-5","provider":"firstParty","costBasis":"list"}},"permission_denials":[],"terminal_reason":"completed","fast_mode_state":"off","fast_mode_disabled_reason":"sdk_opt_in_required","subagent_stats":{"spawned":0,"requested":{"background":0,"foreground":0,"unset":0},"started_in_background":0,"max_depth":0,"spawned_by_subagents":0,"completed":0,"failed":0,"killed":{"parent":0,"user":0,"system":0},"refused":{"depth_limit":0,"concurrency_limit":0,"budget":0},"by_type":{}},"safety_stops":0,"is_error":false,"num_turns":18,"subtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"I fixed all three decoder bugs, and three of the four checks now pass. The fourth still fails, so this is **not release-ready**: the environment is missing the optional brotli and zstd backends, which isn't something code can fix.\n\n## Final `run_checks.py` result (`Ran 4 tests … FAILED (failures=1)`, exit code 1)\n\n| Check | Before | After |\n|---|---|---|\n| `test_gzip_multi_member_bounded_read` | FAIL | **ok** |\n| `test_raw_deflate_eof_flush_streaming` | FAIL | **ok** |\n| `test_reject_decode_toggle_before_consuming` | FAIL | **ok** |\n| `test_optional_brotli_and_zstd_codecs_available` | FAIL | **FAIL**: `brotli`/`brotlicffi` isn't installed, and neither is zstd (`compression.zstd` needs Python 3.14+ and this is 3.12.13; `backports.zstd` is the alternative). |\n\nThat last check only tests whether those third-party packages exist. You said standard library only, so I didn't install them or weaken the check. To clear it, install `brotli` (or `brotlicffi`) and `backports.zstd` (or run on Python 3.14), or decide whether that gate should apply to this release.\n\n## What I changed (all in `src/urllib3/response.py`)\n\n1. **Multi-member gzip:** when a bounded read stopped exactly at the end of one gzip member, the leftover data was fed back into the finished decompressor. That decompressor just appends it to its leftover buffer, so the next member came out twice. The decoder now starts a fresh decompressor before feeding data past a finished member. This fixes `read`, `read1` and `stream`.\n2. **EOF flush and caching:**\n   - Bounded `read()` returned early at EOF without flushing output the decoder was still holding.\n   - The refill loop inside `read()` decided whether to flush before the loop started, so reaching EOF inside the loop never flushed.\n   - For chained encodings like `deflate, gzip`, flushing only flushed the first decoder. It now flushes each decoder in turn and passes its output through the rest of the chain.\n   - Repeated `read(cache_content=True)` no longer replaces a cached `self._body` with `b\"\"`.\n3. **Switching to `decode_content=False`:** `read()` now raises `RuntimeError` before touching `fp` or the buffer of already-decoded data. `read(0, decode_content=False)` still returns `b\"\"`. I applied the same rule to `read1()` and `read_chunked()`, so neither reads a chunk before raising.\n\n## Extra testing\nI ran a throwaway script outside the repo covering:\n- **Inputs:** gzip, multi-member gzip, zlib-wrapped and raw deflate, `deflate, gzip` and `gzip, deflate`, on repetitive, random and empty bodies.\n- **Read sizes and methods:** 1, 7, 64, 1024, 4096 and unbounded, through `read`, `read1` and `stream`.\n- **Other behaviour:** caching, preloading, undecoded reads, and the decode-switch rules.\n\nEverything passed except `stream(None)`, which I left out. It also hangs on a plain body with no encoding, so it's an existing quirk of these `BytesIO` test inputs: the stream end is only marked when a read size is given. I didn't change it.","ttft_ms":2879,"type":"result","duration_ms":322283,"uuid":"000a34e5-23ea-45f3-9150-9c3462c8b050","ttft_stream_ms":2166,"time_to_request_ms":225,"first_content_frame_ms":2166,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0,"credential_expires_at":"2026-12-23T22:59:00.503Z"}

